{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "2: Integrate Assistant0 with Auth0",
  "nextTour": "3: Set up a Google project",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Assistant0",
      "description": "## About Assistant0\n\nAssistant0 is built in Node Express. This Codespace container already installed all the needed dependencies, including the [Auth0 express-openid-connect middleware](https://github.com/auth0/express-openid-connect), which is used to implement authentication with Auth0. This part has already been done for you since the focus of this lab is to integrate tools with the agent so that the agent can perform tasks via third-party APIs on the authenticated user's behalf. \n\nFor the agentic AI implementation we use [Vercel AI](https://auth0.com/ai/docs/sdks/vercel-ai-sdk)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Understanding the code",
      "description": "## Understanding the code\n\nThis is the application structure:\n```\nsrc/\n├── app.ts                  # Express server — routes, OIDC middleware, chat endpoint\n├── lib/\n│   ├── auth0.ts            # AsyncLocalStorage store + getRefreshToken() helper\n│   └── auth0-ai.ts         # You will modify this to include Auth0 AI SDK initialization, withGmailRead/Write wrappers\n├── tools/\n│   └── gmail.ts            # Vercel AI SDK tool definitions for Gmail search and compose\n└── public/\n    ├── index.html          # Single-page chat UI\n    └── app.js              # Vanilla JS — session check, SSE stream reader, pop-up authorization\n```"
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/.env.local",
      "description": "## Update `.env.local` - generate an application secret\n\nNow let's generate a secret to encode the values.\n\n1. Select [this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"openssl rand -hex 32\"]) to run the command `openssl rand -hex 32` in the terminal.\n\n2. Copy the output and update the value of the `AUTH0_SECRET` variable highlighted on the line above.",
      "line": 5,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 5,
          "character": 15
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 5,
          "character": 70
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Update `.env.local` - Set the app base URL",
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/.env.local",
      "description": "## Update `.env.local` - Set the app base URL\n\nIn order to configure the app to work properly in the Codespace you need to set the base URL.\n\n1. [Select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev\"]) to run the command on the terminal.\n2. Copy the output and update the `APP_BASE_URL` with that value.\n\n-----\n\nAfter the update your APP_BASE_URL should look something like this:\n\n```\nAPP_BASE_URL=\"https://humble-winner-74xv5jxw462r9pv-3000.app.github.dev\"\n```",
      "line": 6,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 6,
          "character": 15
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 6,
          "character": 32
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Create an Auth0 application integration",
      "description": "## Create an Auth0 application integration\n\n1. Go to the [Auth0 Dashboard](https://manage.auth0.com/#/applications). And create and configure an Auth0 Application with the following properties:\n\n    - Name: **Assistant0**\n    - Type: **Regular Web**\n\n2. Then select the **Settings** tab on your Assistant0 page.\n\n3. Scroll down to **Application URIs** and configure the following:\n\n    * In the **Allowed Callback URLs**: [Select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo \\\"https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev/auth/callback\\\"\"]) and copy the output\n    * In the **Allowed Logout URLs**: [Select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo \\\"https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev/\\\"\"]) and copy the output\n\n4. Select **Save** at the bottom of the page.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 43
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/.env.local",
      "description": "## Update `.env.local` - Domain\n\n1. Still on your application's Settings tab, scroll up to the **Basic Information** section.\n1. Copy the **Domain**.\n1. Paste the Domain value to the line highlighted above to set the `AUTH0_DOMAIN` variable. Ensure you **don't** have a `https://` otherwise the connection with Gmail later will fail.",
      "line": 7,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 7,
          "character": 15
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 7,
          "character": 27
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/.env.local",
      "description": "## Update `.env.local` - Client ID\n\n1. From your application's Setting tab, copy the **Client ID**.\n1. Paste the Client ID to the line highlighted above to set the `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID` variable.",
      "line": 8,
