    {
      "title": "Enable Google connection",
      "description": "## Enable Google connection\n\n1. In the Auth0 dashboard, go to the **Connections** tab.\n2. Ensure that only the **google-oauth2** connection is enabled."
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable My Account API",
      "description": "## Enable My Account API\n\nOur AI app will ultimately be able to retreive third-party API tokens using the [Connected Accounts](https://auth0.com/docs/secure/call-apis-on-users-behalf/token-vault/connected-accounts-for-token-vault) flow. This flow relies on the [My Account API](https://auth0.com/docs/manage-users/my-account-api), which is early access, so we will have to manually enable it on the tenant. These steps will create a client grant that allows Assistant0 to access the My Account API with the Connected Accounts scopes on the user’s behalf.\n\n1. From the Auth0 Dashboard, got to **Applications > APIs**.\n2. From the My Account API banner, select **Activate**.\n3. Now that it's activated, select **Auth0 My Account API** and then select the **Application Access** tab.\n4. Select the **Edit** link corresponding to Assistant0 to configure its application access policies.\n5. Grant access to the Assistant0 application.\n6. Select **All** permissions and the application grant access.\n8. Still on the Auth0 My Account API page, go to the **Settings** tab. \n9. Under Access Settings, toggle on **Allow Skipping User Consent**.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 2,
          "character": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Test the app",
      "description": "## Test the Assistant0 app\n\nWe haven't yet integrated our Gmail tool, but we can run the app to ensure it works with our OpenAI API key.\n\n1. Select [this link](command:workbench.action.debug.start) to run the application. \n\n1. Select the **Open in Browser** in the dialog that appears in the bottom right corner to visit your app's URL. \n>If you miss the dialog, you can always select the **PORTS** tab below next to **TERMINAL** and then hover over the **FORWARDED ADDRESS** and select the globe icon to open your app's URL.\n\n1. Sign up for the application using Google. This will be necessary for when we integrate the Gmail tool.\n\n1. Once logged into Assistant0, test that your OpenAPI key works by asking \"What can you help me with?\"\n    > Note: You should see a response listing Assistant0's intended uses; however, since we have not yet integrated tooling to our application, the agent does not yet have the capability to perform tasks requiring Google API permissions on your behalf just yet.\n\n1. Log out of the application.\n1. Select [this link](command:workbench.action.debug.stop) to stop the application.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
